        "text": "Viștea Mare (Romanian pronunciation: [ˈviʃte̯a ˈmare]) is a mountain peak in the Făgăraș Mountains of the Southern Carpathians of Brașov County in Romania. With an elevation of 2,527 metres (8,291 ft), it is the third highest peak in Romania after Moldoveanu Peak (2,544 m) and Negoiu Peak (2,535 m).\n\n\n== External links ==\nVistea Mare Peak and many other photos from the Romanian Carpathians Archived 2009-06-18 at the Wayback Machine\n(in Romanian and English)  Salvamontvictoria.com",
